.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/esutils Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "esutils [![Build Status](https://secure.travis-ci.org/estools/esutils.svg)](http://travis-ci.org/estools/esutils)"
.PP
esutils (\fResutils\fP) is utility box for ECMAScript language tools\&.
.SS "API"
.SS "ast"
.SS "ast\&.isExpression(node)"
Returns true if \fRnode\fP is an Expression as defined in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 section \fR11\fP\&.
.SS "ast\&.isStatement(node)"
Returns true if \fRnode\fP is a Statement as defined in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 section \fR12\fP\&.
.SS "ast\&.isIterationStatement(node)"
Returns true if \fRnode\fP is an IterationStatement as defined in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 section \fR12\&.6\fP\&.
.SS "ast\&.isSourceElement(node)"
Returns true if \fRnode\fP is a SourceElement as defined in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 section \fR14\fP\&.
.SS "ast\&.trailingStatement(node)"
Returns \fRStatement?\fP if \fRnode\fP has trailing \fRStatement\fP\&. 
.PP
.nf
if (cond)
    consequent;

.fi
.PP
 When taking this \fRIfStatement\fP, returns \fRconsequent;\fP statement\&.
.SS "ast\&.isProblematicIfStatement(node)"
Returns true if \fRnode\fP is a problematic IfStatement\&. If \fRnode\fP is a problematic \fRIfStatement\fP, \fRnode\fP cannot be represented as an one on one JavaScript code\&. 
.PP
.nf
{
    type: 'IfStatement',
    consequent: {
        type: 'WithStatement',
        body: {
            type: 'IfStatement',
            consequent: {type: 'EmptyStatement'}
        }
    },
    alternate: {type: 'EmptyStatement'}
}

.fi
.PP
 The above node cannot be represented as a JavaScript code, since the top level \fRelse\fP alternate belongs to an inner \fRIfStatement\fP\&.
.SS "code"
.SS "code\&.isDecimalDigit(code)"
Return true if provided code is decimal digit\&.
.SS "code\&.isHexDigit(code)"
Return true if provided code is hexadecimal digit\&.
.SS "code\&.isOctalDigit(code)"
Return true if provided code is octal digit\&.
.SS "code\&.isWhiteSpace(code)"
Return true if provided code is white space\&. White space characters are formally defined in ECMA262\&.
.SS "code\&.isLineTerminator(code)"
Return true if provided code is line terminator\&. Line terminator characters are formally defined in ECMA262\&.
.SS "code\&.isIdentifierStart(code)"
Return true if provided code can be the first character of ECMA262 Identifier\&. They are formally defined in ECMA262\&.
.SS "code\&.isIdentifierPart(code)"
Return true if provided code can be the trailing character of ECMA262 Identifier\&. They are formally defined in ECMA262\&.
.SS "keyword"
.SS "keyword\&.isKeywordES5(id, strict)"
Returns \fRtrue\fP if provided identifier string is a Keyword or Future Reserved Word in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1\&. They are formally defined in ECMA262 sections \fR7\&.6\&.1\&.1\fP and \fR7\&.6\&.1\&.2\fP, respectively\&. If the \fRstrict\fP flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether \fRid\fP is a Keyword or Future Reserved Word under strict mode\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isKeywordES6(id, strict)"
Returns \fRtrue\fP if provided identifier string is a Keyword or Future Reserved Word in ECMA262 edition 6\&. They are formally defined in ECMA262 sections \fR11\&.6\&.2\&.1\fP and \fR11\&.6\&.2\&.2\fP, respectively\&. If the \fRstrict\fP flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether \fRid\fP is a Keyword or Future Reserved Word under strict mode\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isReservedWordES5(id, strict)"
Returns \fRtrue\fP if provided identifier string is a Reserved Word in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1\&. They are formally defined in ECMA262 section \fR7\&.6\&.1\fP\&. If the \fRstrict\fP flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether \fRid\fP is a Reserved Word under strict mode\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isReservedWordES6(id, strict)"
Returns \fRtrue\fP if provided identifier string is a Reserved Word in ECMA262 edition 6\&. They are formally defined in ECMA262 section \fR11\&.6\&.2\fP\&. If the \fRstrict\fP flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether \fRid\fP is a Reserved Word under strict mode\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isRestrictedWord(id)"
Returns \fRtrue\fP if provided identifier string is one of \fReval\fP or \fRarguments\fP\&. They are restricted in strict mode code throughout ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 and in ECMA262 edition 6 section \fR12\&.1\&.1\fP\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isIdentifierNameES5(id)"
Return true if provided identifier string is an IdentifierName as specified in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 section \fR7\&.6\fP\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isIdentifierNameES6(id)"
Return true if provided identifier string is an IdentifierName as specified in ECMA262 edition 6 section \fR11\&.6\fP\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isIdentifierES5(id, strict)"
Return true if provided identifier string is an Identifier as specified in ECMA262 edition 5\&.1 section \fR7\&.6\fP\&. If the \fRstrict\fP flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether \fRid\fP is an Identifier under strict mode\&.
.SS "keyword\&.isIdentifierES6(id, strict)"
Return true if provided identifier string is an Identifier as specified in ECMA262 edition 6 section \fR12\&.1\fP\&. If the \fRstrict\fP flag is truthy, this function additionally checks whether \fRid\fP is an Identifier under strict mode\&.
